### 4.1 Why this layout

- **`.kiro/steering/`** is project memory — always loaded by the agent before any task.
- **`.kiro/settings/`** is the *style guide* for how the agent generates artifacts. Treat it as code-reviewed configuration.
- **`.kiro/settings/mcp.json`** is workspace-scope MCP. User-scope MCP lives in `~/.kiro/settings/mcp.json`.
- **`.kiro/specs/`** is the living technical history of every approved contract.
- **`.agents/skills/`** (or platform-specific equivalent: `.claude/skills/`, `.cursor/skills/`) contains the executable workflow as installable skills.
- **`CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md`** is the entry-point that tells any compatible agent where to find the workflow.

### 4.2 Minimum per-repository checklist

Every repository that uses Kiro SHALL have, at a minimum:

- `.kiro/steering/{product,tech,structure}.md`
- `.kiro/steering/{security,testing,api-conventions}.md` for any non-trivial codebase
- `.kiroignore` configured with secrets and credentials
- `.kiro/settings/mcp.json` declaring only the project-specific MCPs that are reviewed and approved
- Entry-point file (`CLAUDE.md` or `AGENTS.md`) describing the workflow and pointing to this document

