| `kiro-verify-completion` | Fresh-evidence gate before any completion claim. |

### 8.9 Skill authoring checklist

**Before writing a skill:**

- [ ] Real expertise captured (hands-on task or synthesized artifacts).
- [ ] Scope defined as a coherent unit of work.
- [ ] Inputs, outputs, and triggers identified.
- [ ] At least one concrete test case ready.

**During authoring:**

- [ ] `SKILL.md` under 500 lines / 5,000 tokens.
- [ ] No content the agent already knows from general training.
- [ ] Defaults chosen; alternatives mentioned briefly.
- [ ] Specificity calibrated to fragility (prescriptive where fragile, flexible where not).
- [ ] Gotchas section present for non-obvious facts.
- [ ] Output templates where format matters.
- [ ] Triggers for `references/` files are explicit ("Read X when Y").

**After authoring:**

- [ ] Skill run against at least one real task.
- [ ] Execution trace reviewed, not just final output.
- [ ] False positives, missed cases, and dead instructions identified.
- [ ] Gotchas added for every correction made during the run.
- [ ] Repeated logic refactored into `scripts/`.

