## 23. Compliance summary

This document is the canonical specification for any Kiro workflow developed by the team. By the time a workflow is delivered, the following SHALL be true:

- All steering files exist with the correct inclusion modes.
- All specs use EARS for requirements and the boundary-annotated format for tasks.
- All skills conform to the `SKILL.md` template, the 500-line limit, and the progressive-disclosure rule for references.
- All MCP servers are reviewed, scoped, and free of versioned credentials.
- All hooks declare a single responsibility and either run idempotent shell commands or contextual Agent Prompts.
- All custom agents declare the smallest tool scope required.
- `.kiroignore` is in place and covers secrets, customer data, and large artifacts.
- All PRs link back to a Spec or document why no Spec was required.
- Approvals in `spec.json` reflect actual human review at each phase gate.

Any workflow that does not meet these requirements is not considered production-ready under this specification.

